WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.580 --> 00:00:04.180
At the end of September, Amazon Prime Video
will make sure its subscribers are ready for

00:00:04.180 --> 00:00:04.680
Halloween.

00:00:04.820 --> 00:00:09.420
The last day of the month will see the addition
of scary flicks like Cloverfield, Event Horizon,

00:00:09.420 --> 00:00:11.260
and Tales from the Darkside: The Movie.

00:00:11.440 --> 00:00:15.490
Maybe because of the big influx, Prime isn't
adding quite as many movies and TV shows in

00:00:15.490 --> 00:00:19.020
October, but what the line-up lacks in quantity,
it makes up for in quality.

00:00:19.180 --> 00:00:23.340
As of October 2019, the Amazon Prime original
Goliath will be three years old.

00:00:23.780 --> 00:00:25.040
"I hate you very much."

00:00:25.640 --> 00:00:26.920
"I hate you too, honey."

00:00:27.730 --> 00:00:31.780
The first season of the legal drama starring
Billy Bob Thornton as a washed-up lawyer seeking

00:00:31.780 --> 00:00:34.940
to atone for past mistakes premiered in October
2016.

00:00:35.160 --> 00:00:39.200
Fans had to wait two years for a second season,
and fortunately, they only had to wait half

00:00:39.200 --> 00:00:40.180
the time for a third.

00:00:40.380 --> 00:00:44.880
At the end of October, the 1993 crime film
Killing Zoe is heading to Prime Video.

00:00:45.040 --> 00:00:48.690
Eric Stoltz stars in this American-French
film in the vein of early Quentin Tarantino

00:00:48.690 --> 00:00:49.720
films of the time.

00:00:49.920 --> 00:00:53.240
Earlier in the month, however, we'll get a
decidedly different kind of film.

00:00:53.250 --> 00:00:57.010
October 1st brings the 2009 animated film
Astro Boy to Prime.

00:00:57.010 --> 00:01:00.680
Astro Boy follows the adventures of a young
boy who's killed, and then resurrected as

00:01:00.680 --> 00:01:01.800
a robot superhero.

00:01:02.300 --> 00:01:06.120
It may have been tough at first to imagine
John Krasinski as an action hero, but Prime's

00:01:06.120 --> 00:01:10.460
original Jack Ryan changed that in a big way
when Krasinski took on the role of Tom Clancy's

00:01:10.460 --> 00:01:12.100
most recognizable protagonist.

00:01:12.220 --> 00:01:15.320
Jack Ryan isn't the first time the hero has
been adapted to the screen.

00:01:15.810 --> 00:01:20.160
Harrison Ford played the CIA analyst twice,
beginning with the espionage thriller Patriot

00:01:20.160 --> 00:01:22.920
Games, which is set to arrive on Prime on
October 1st.

00:01:23.070 --> 00:01:27.400
In this 1992 film, Ryan is thrust into the
role of hero when — while on vacation in

00:01:27.400 --> 00:01:30.620
London — he witnesses an attack on members
of the English royal family.

00:01:30.870 --> 00:01:34.580
Ryan — who'd left the CIA before the events
of the film — returns to his former job

00:01:34.580 --> 00:01:37.140
so he can take the reins of the efforts to
capture the terrorist.

00:01:37.360 --> 00:01:41.120
"I will put such a strange hold on your gun
money that you'll be out on the street throwing

00:01:41.120 --> 00:01:41.620
rocks."

00:01:42.400 --> 00:01:45.500
Adding to the already long list of horror
titles being added to Prime at the end of

00:01:45.500 --> 00:01:48.680
September, October 3rd brings High Life to
the streaming service.

00:01:48.900 --> 00:01:53.380
Starring Robert Pattinson and Juliette Binoche,
High Life is a sci-fi/horror film following

00:01:53.380 --> 00:01:55.860
a group of convicts sent to explore a Black
Hole.

00:01:56.340 --> 00:02:00.140
Haley Joel Osment, who initially won widespread
recognition as the boy who could "see dead

00:02:00.150 --> 00:02:03.720
people" in M. Night Shyamalan's The Sixth
Sense, has been enjoying some prominent roles

00:02:03.720 --> 00:02:06.180
in recent series like Future Man and The Boys.

00:02:06.380 --> 00:02:09.479
But if you'd like a chance to see him back
when he was beardless, Prime offers the chance

00:02:09.479 --> 00:02:12.319
on October 1st, when it adds Steven Spielberg's
A.I.

00:02:12.320 --> 00:02:14.120
Artificial Intelligence to its library.

00:02:14.350 --> 00:02:18.300
Set in the not-too-distant future, A.I. is
about a young robot boy whose programming

00:02:18.300 --> 00:02:20.080
somehow allows for the capacity to love.

00:02:20.420 --> 00:02:24.740
Jude Law stars alongside Osment as Gigolo
Joe, a robot sex worker on the run.

00:02:24.940 --> 00:02:29.140
While Prime's original Goliath brings us a
fresh mystery in October, later in the month,

00:02:29.140 --> 00:02:33.150
the streaming service will add the third season
of the British crime drama Unforgotten, which

00:02:33.150 --> 00:02:36.140
focuses on mysteries so old that everyone
else has given up on them.

00:02:36.220 --> 00:02:40.700
In Unforgotten's third season, Detective Chief
Inspector Cassie Stuart and her partner Sunny

00:02:40.700 --> 00:02:42.800
tackle a case almost two decades old.

00:02:43.240 --> 00:02:46.440
"DCI Cass Stuart and DI Sunny Khan."

00:02:46.880 --> 00:02:50.440
When workers on a highway uncover the remains
of a 16 year old girl who was reported missing

00:02:50.440 --> 00:02:52.660
in 2000, it gets the heroes' attention.

00:02:52.849 --> 00:02:56.840
Unforgotten's fourth season has been confirmed,
and it's likely for release either later this

00:02:56.840 --> 00:02:58.180
year or in 2020.

00:02:58.440 --> 00:03:01.870
If you're a Prime subscriber looking to get
caught up for the upcoming season, this looks

00:03:01.870 --> 00:03:03.480
like the perfect opportunity.

